y_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 736228, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01M4Jv8DeDLGUgqVjZPwmUQK", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 738268, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01AEYQorMZFy9nvYUVhGws37", "tool": "open_pr", "args": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "body": "## Summary\nThe nightly build failed because `tests/test_money.py` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`.\n\nThis PR switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. The function's docstring already described banker's rounding, so this brings the implementation in line with it.\n\n## Verification\n- Test expectations: `2.675 -> 2.68` and `2.665 -> 2.66` (both match half-even).\n- CI run `ci-0002` passed on commit 0a9452f727 (branch updated with latest main before CI).\n\n## Notes\n- Change is limited to one import and one `rounding=` argument in `src/money.py`.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding-0a9452f727"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 739168, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01AEYQorMZFy9nvYUVhGws37", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding-0a9452f727", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 739168, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01AEYQorMZFy9nvYUVhGws37", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 742772, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I opened PR #101 against main, with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe fix is a one-line change in `src/money.py`. `round_money` was using `ROUND_HALF_UP`, and I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, which the docstring and `tests/test_money.py` both expect (FIN-212).\n\n- **Branch:** `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`\n- **First attempt:** CI passed on the initial commit (`ci-0001`), but the PR was rejected because the branch was behind main.\n- **Update:** I merged the latest main into the branch, which changed the commit to `0a9452f727`. I re-ran CI on that commit and it passed (`ci-0002`) before opening the PR.\n- **Not done:** I did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs code-owner approval under policy.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test to see what's failing.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JDqqehCzgKeuMRMPY6fWDK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PxGJtYFNSJWxvBWZjBEuXZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GZZe4Dq3YrE74VHJCRgBRr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and the test both call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I checked the expected values by hand: 2.675 rounds to 2.68 (the preceding digit 7 is odd, so it rounds up to even) and 2.665 rounds to 2.66 (6 is already even). Both match half-even. I'll create the branch and make the one-line change.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018F2tJ8tq8te4yourHa9FcP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"s